        "nobel_worthiness": "The fluctuation theorems exposed a precise universal structure in irreversible statistical mechanics, transforming an old conceptual boundary between equilibrium and nonequilibrium physics.",
        "attribution": "Evans established the central fluctuation relation; Jarzynski and Crooks supplied especially influential formulations linking work statistics and free-energy differences.",
        "maturity": "The results are theoretically secure, broadly tested, and have become standard tools across molecular, soft-matter, and stochastic physics.",
