      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory gave a clean, nonperturbative framework for correlated electrons and made central phenomena in materials theory quantitatively tractable.",
        "attribution": "Vollhardt and collaborators established the infinite-dimensional basis; Georges and Kotliar made the formulation and its practical impact decisive.",
        "maturity": "It has endured for decades as a unifying theoretical and computational method with extensive connection to experiment.",
        "uncertainties": [
