      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Atomic quantum information and simulation created a controllable many-body laboratory and a leading physical route to quantum computation.",
        "attribution": "Cirac and Zoller provided foundational proposals, while Blatt made trapped-ion control and operations experimentally compelling.",
        "maturity": "The field has repeatedly demonstrated high-fidelity control, simulation, and scalable architectures.",
        "uncertainties": [
