        "Alexei Kitaev",
        "Peter W. Shor",
        "Andrew M. Steane"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum error correction identified the essential mechanism by which fragile quantum information can be protected and made fault tolerant.",
        "attribution": "Shor, Steane, and Kitaev each introduced foundational and complementary coding ideas central to the field.",
        "maturity": "The principles are now experimentally realized and indispensable to credible large-scale quantum computing.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Credit extends across a broad community and selecting only three founders is intrinsically difficult."
